{"name":"Gentleman’s Whiskey","hex":"#ca882c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gentleman","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any well-bred, well-mannered, or charming man.","Any man."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gentleman"},{"term":"whiskey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Whiskey of the ICAO/NATO radiotelephony alphabet."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A liquor distilled from the fermented mash of grain (as rye, corn, or barley).","A drink of whiskey."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/whiskey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Whisky","blocks":[{"text":"Whisky or whiskey is a type of liquor made from fermented grain mash. Various grains are used for different varieties, including barley, corn, rye, and wheat. Whisky is typically aged in wooden casks, commonly of charred white oak. Uncharred white oak casks previously used for the aging of port, rum, or sherry may be employed during storage to impart a unique flavour and colour."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Whiskyhogmanay2010.jpg/330px-Whiskyhogmanay2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Whisky","wikidata":"Q281"},{"title":"Gentleman","blocks":[{"text":"A gentleman is a chivalrous, courteous, or honourable man. Originally, gentleman was the lowest rank of the landed gentry of England, ranking below an esquire and above a yeoman; by definition, the rank of gentleman comprised the younger sons of the younger sons of peers, and the younger sons of a baronet, a knight, and an esquire, in perpetual succession. As such, the connotation of the term gentleman captures the common denominator of gentility ; a right shared by the peerage and the gentry, the constituent classes of the British nobility."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/The_English_Gentleman_Richard_Brathwait_by_Robert_Vaughan_1630.jpg/330px-The_English_Gentleman_Richard_Brathwait_by_Robert_Vaughan_1630.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gentleman","wikidata":"Q749212"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg/500px-Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg/1280px-Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg/500px-Distillerie_OldBushmills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Old Bushmills Distillery, County Antrim","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADistillerie_OldBushmills.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg/500px-Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg/1280px-Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg/500px-Erskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_%281869%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man pours some whisky into a flask in this 1869 oil painting by Scottish artist Erskine Nicol.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AErskine_Nicol%2C_A_Nip_against_the_Cold_(1869).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu